TITLE: Design and Implementation of a Multi-Agent Threat Intelligence Assistant Based on Generative AI
KEYWORDS: Cyber Threat Intelligence; Cybersecurity; Generative AI; LLM; Computation theory; Cybersecurity; Knowledge based systems; Open systems; Cybe threat intelligence; Cyber security; Cyber threats; Daily activity; Design and implementations; Generative AI; Language model; Large language model; Multi agent; Open source intelligence; Multi agent systems
ABSTRACT: Cyber threat intelligence programs are designed to support the daily activities of cybersecurity analysts. However, most of the existing tools are unable to provide accurate information. To fill this gap and provide analysts with verified data, we propose an interactive assistant leveraging generative AI techniques and large language models (LLMs) to identify and categorize information related to threat actors based on open-source intelligence (OSINT). Users can interact with the assistant through a simple chat interface, asking questions in natural language. Based on the user's question, the assistant (i) queries a large knowledge base containing information about numerous threat actors collected from multiple OSINT sources and (ii) processes the response to make it comprehensible to the end user. The assistant, enabled with LLM capabilities, can also be used to generate summaries from cybersecurity research reports or extract specific information from them. A preliminary evaluation, conducted with experts in the field, demonstrates the effectiveness of the proposed assistant in supporting the daily activities of cyber threat analysts. © 2025 IEEE.
